WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.770
It's finally the second semester.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:09.230
Now, it's time to present your summer 
break free research projects.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.180
First, Yayoi-san.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.130
I was fortunate enough to be tutored by an acquaintance of my father's

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.490
who is a famous cultural expert.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.820
Using traditional Japanese 
crafting techniques,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.270
I created a Disfia Foreigner in the 
form of wooden mosaic artwork.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.000
Wow. That's amazing.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.950
That's not very student-like.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.070
Is there some kind of problem?

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.340
No, it's fine.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.610
Next we have Karin-san and Karen-san.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.180
I'm told you worked together on your project?

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.000
Um... What is this?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.790
Please wait a moment.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.820
I'm almost done making it into 
a Tritomy-like Foreigner robot.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.100
I'm drinking for it right now.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.240
I apologize. I was negligent 
in supervising them.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.990
Moving on. Next we have Lion-san.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.080
What's this? A wooden carving of a bear?

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.370
Yup. Daddy taught me how 
to carve it with a knife.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.890
You managed to produce this level 
of quality with one knife?

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.110
That's amazing all on its own.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.340
Isn't the salmon in its 
mouth a little too big?

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.500
Well it's a tuna!

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.640
Tuna?

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.720
Why tuna?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.720
Because I love tuna!

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.450
I-I see.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.600
All right, next we have Nina-san.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.310
Um? What's this?

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.730
I measured the pulses of a Cepheid 
variable star

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.000
and observed the distance between other 
astronomical objects outside of our galaxy.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.690
In addition, I collected data on 
the expansion of the universe.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.950
Good. Next.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.110
Um, next is...

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.420
She can't wait.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.540
It's like she can't contain herself anymore.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>I've got a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.430
I suppose I'll ask.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.260
What's this?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.120
You got it! It's a new 
model of a Powered Suit

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.780
that allows a normal human 
to enter a Paradox Zone!

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.170
If we can perfect these suits,

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:36.030
people other than Logicalists should 
be able to enter Paradox Zones,

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.530
and can do things like save injured people, 
or whatever they'd like to do in those zones!

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.680
And someday, we'll be able to use
these suits to visit Septpia!

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:48.540
Iyokan

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:45.730
Is this cardboard?

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.540
I ran out of time making the backpack.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.800
But I spent so long making it, 
so let's see it in action.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.460
No! How about another time?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.800
Why won't you let me try it?

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.260
Oh, that's right!

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.620
There's the student council's information
about the school festival,

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.130
and we still need your class 
to decide on a project leader.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.010
A project leader for the school festival?

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.360
That's right. Someone from the class
who'll help with the festival.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.550
We'll leave the details to you, Yayoi-san.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:18.500
Indeed. The principal asked to see us, so 
we'll talk to you later about your decision.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.730
Once you've decided on everything, 
come see us in the staff office.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:22.740
Later!

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.520
They ran away.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.550
They're leaving everything 
completely in our hands.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.100
Well it's first-year class S.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.000
In any event,

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:35.230
I will take over and we will move forward 
with resolving the matter at hand.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.670
A school announcement?

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.580
<i>Yuko wouldn't even answer calls from me.</i>

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.170
<i>I wonder where she was all summer break,
and what she was doing.</i>

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.450
<i>Home. Home. Home.</i>

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.600
<i>Heart mark?!</i>

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.230
<i>What could this possibly symbolize?</i>

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.670
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.370
<i>President, are you really okay with this?</i>

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.440
<i>The broadcast has already begun.</i>

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.150
<i>What?!</i>

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.190
<i>All you good little girls out there,</i>

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.040
<i>let's keep this a secret from Yuko.</i>

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.340
<i>Huh? Yuko! This isn't what you think!</i>

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.790
What are they even doing?

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.460
<i>I apologize for exposing you 
all to a very unsightly event.</i>

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.050
<i>Now to begin anew,</i>

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.800
<i>our first school festival at Pirari 
Academy is soon approaching.</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.960
<i>Using our coexistence with 
Foreigners as a theme,</i>

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.650
<i>we'd like each class, committee and club to</i>

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.310
<i>come up with ideas of what 
to do during the festival.</i>

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.170
<i>And in order to raise the morale of 
each and every student in the school,</i>

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.690
<i>the student council will run a popularity 
contest between all of the events.</i>

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.320
<i>Let's all aim for first place, and 
make this the best school festival we can.</i>

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.790
<i>That concludes this message 
from your student council.</i>

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.760
<i>Yuko, what you saw was 
really a misunderstanding!</i>

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.210
<i>I was only—</i>

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.740
A popularity contest, huh?

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.860
I wonder if we'll get 
anything for getting first place?

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.260
I'd like an all-you-can-eat buffet.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.480
Before we think about the reward,

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.640
we need to decide on what we will do.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.720
Does anyone have any ideas?

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.860
What kind of things do people 
normally do in school festivals?

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.270
I think we should go with 
the standard maid cafe.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.980
Welcome, my lady.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.940
That'd be cute!

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.860
Or maybe a heart-pounding haunted house!

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.410
All-you-can-eat.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.790
I want to be a zombie!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.410
Right? I think it'd be super exciting!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.730
I reject that.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.210
No? Why not?

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:48.260
Are you actually afraid of ghosts or something?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.700
I can see it.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.010
I-I'm not scared.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.300
It's okay.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.180
Ghosts are nothing to be scared of.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.420
All right, that's enough of that.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.900
Whether or not ghosts exists, 
the idea's rejected!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.080
To begin with, the theme 
for this school festival

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.340
is supposed to be our 
coexistence with Foreigners.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:17.490
We have to do something more academic.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.260
Oh, I get it!

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:24.120
I wonder what would work out well?

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.320
On the topic of Lion,

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.530
I'll be conducting extracurricular 
lessons with her this semester.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:34.850
I will give direct her in resolving
her unstable Trance situation.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:41.960
The fluctuating light that scatters 
will surely appear as fleeting.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.950
You understand, don't you? You should.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.340
Be sure to keep a vigilant eye on her.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:52.450
I will.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:59.660
Maid Cafe
Haunted House
Escape Room
Fried Noodles
Crepes
Bowling
Darts

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.690
Is there anyone else with an idea?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.160
Me!

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:02.600
I think it'd be nice to sing a song!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:03.370
A song?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.130
I was thinking about it during our break.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:10.380
We should all sing the song 
Lion taught us from Monolium.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.690
What? That song?

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.860
We can learn Foreigner culture from songs.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:21.760
It's a perfect match for the theme 
of coexistence with Foreigners!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.430
Certainly, I believe it's a wonderful idea.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:32.820
But we only have the one song 
Lion sang as a Foreigner song.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.610
Isn't that right?

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.950
Can we really convey anything 
with that one song?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.950
Yeah, you've got a point.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.060
Perhaps we can take the 
feelings put into that song

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.260
and come up with a more simple 
way to convey them to everyone.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.460
We can make the song a part of a story.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:55.340
A part of a story? What do you mean?

00:08:58.530 --> 00:08:59.960
I mean a performance!

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.250
Like a play!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.850
A play?

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:08.580
This sounds like it'll be fun!

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.370
What will the story be about?

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.530
Beats me.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:18.280
Lion, sing the song for them 
once so they can all understand!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:22.370
This thing's got a karaoke mode, too.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:26.870
Wow! It can light up!

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.380
Look! My tea stem is floating upright.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.900
That's great.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.520
But I don't intend to forgive you 
for that invasion of privacy.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.020
A-Anyway, the only group 
that hasn't submitted their

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.840
documentation to us yet 
is first-year class S.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.790
You know what kind of children they are.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.020
They're surely just exploding with—

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.300
It looks like it might take a while longer.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:55.030
Yeah.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:03.240
A play using a Foreigner song.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.380
What a fresh idea.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:09.210
So? Who's going to write the story?

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.710
I came up with it, so I'll write it!

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.730
What kind of story will it be?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.860
I haven't thought of anything yet.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.180
Really?!

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:18.980
I figured...

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:19.720
Huh?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.970
Year 1 Class S has decided on a 
play using a Foreigner song.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.970
Project Leader:  Mahiro Kyobashi

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.970
It says the leader is Mahiro-san.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.810
Huh? That's a mistake.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.490
The class representative Ya-chan will—

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:30.090
No. You do it, Mahiro-san.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:30.980
Wha?

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.340
Excuse us.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.340
<b>Teacher's Room</b>

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.250
Now I'm the leader all of a sudden...

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:41.890
That's way too much responsibility.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.990
I thought you'd do it, Ya-chan.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:49.210
Originally I also thought I'd be the leader.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.670
But after listening to you,

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.530
I felt that it was something you had to do.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.640
Hiro-chan.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:03.640
I just felt that the person who feels most 
passionately about Foreigners should be in charge.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.140
I can't think of anything good to write!

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:25.200
Mahiro-chan's giving it her all.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:35.520
Whoever said the god of scenario 
writing would visit me, fight me!

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:36.630
<b>That's right. A god of scenario writing exists. 
All you have to do is wait for him to visit you.</b>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.980
What's most amazing is she 
thinks we won't figure her out.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:58.970
She even went out of her way 
to paint her eyes in.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:00.440
She really gave it her all.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.450
That's what's most important?

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.330
I bet she's tired because she 
spent all her time building that.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.070
Hey, Mahiro here!

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:16.470
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.340
The two of us together make...

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.370
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.570
Come on!

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.920
Or that's the shtick we have going on.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.630
Robo-Girl comes from Tritomy.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.560
Go ahead and give a little 
intro for yourself.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:30.720
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:34.000
Jeez, all you ever say is "Robo-Girl"!

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.410
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.670
You sure are stiff.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:40.210
Wonder what kind of people live on Tritomy.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.970
I'd like to meet 'em one day.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:44.740
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.740
Come on! You sound like 
some kind of broken robot.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.490
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.520
Had that one coming!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.780
Even your body's stiff!

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:57.090
<i>Robo-Girl.</i>

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.480
Mahiro-san!

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:14.020
Today we'll have a mock battle with the four 
of you who possess multiple covenants.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.740
I'm sleepy.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.400
First off, let's have you Trance.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.320
Got it!

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:23.580
Got it!

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:29.120
This will be our first battle, Nagi!

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.620
<i>Do you think you can handle my power?</i>

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.320
Gate Access! Tritomy!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.920
Dread, let's do this with a bang!

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:58.060
<i>Sounds good! Go get 'em.</i>

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.300
I Tranced! Yay!

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.920
Then it's time to start the mock battle.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:24.210
Yayoi and Mahiro. Ready?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:24.920
Yup!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:32.200
This is my version of a wake-up call!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.810
Messy shots like that will never hit me.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:42.640
Hey lady! Play with me!

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:45.730
Next. Nina and Lion. Start.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.400
I'll do my best!

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.240
I'm not gonna lose!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:14:59.410
<i>She's fast.</i>

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.220
<i>But I'm not going to go along with this.</i>

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.420
Trance Change!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.770
If that's the card you'll 
play, I'll join you.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.890
Trance Change!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.620
Nothing less.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.090
Waffle-chan.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:49.920
I was hopeful about pairing you with 
a childish Foreigner like Waffle.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:53.090
Your ability to empathize with 
Foreigners is something else, huh?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.680
Miss Kagura, what should I do?

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.870
Train both your heart and body.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.190
Let's see...

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.670
From now on we'll have regular 
extracurricular lessons.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:08.440
We'll have one-on-one combat training.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.190
How do I train my heart?

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.070
That's a good question.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:24.840
And?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.800
As I thought. You're sensitive 
to other people's feelings too.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.800
Did I scare you?

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.620
Um? Just a bit.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.110
Look in the mirror.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.390
With a threat as small as 
that, your emotions run wild.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.770
And the balance in your Trance collapses.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:48.770
What I intend to have you train with me 
is not limited to your body and skills.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.190
It includes your heart as well.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.640
Understand?

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:53.960
Yeah.

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:02.320
Miss Kagura.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:09.110
What does it mean to be a strong Logicalist?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.630
Why do you ask?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:18.520
Um... I know this girl, and she's really 
strong, but she has to get even stronger.

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:19.720
Or more like...

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:24.140
She has to prove that she's strong?

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:25.940
Yeah?

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:31.730
I tried to think about it a lot, 
but I didn't get it at all.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:34.520
I want to cheer her on.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:37.490
I want to help, even if it's just a bit.

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.870
Then stay by her side.

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:46.420
Anyone would feel stupid worrying 
about things when they look at you.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.750
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.540
I wonder how I can make it back to ALCA.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:15.740
The god of scenario writing won't visit me.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:21.310
God! Buddha! Or if that's 
too much, even an angel.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.160
Please come to me.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.370
An angel?

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.590
I know. This is it. This is it!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:49.600
God has come to me! No, more like 
an angel and a flower sprite!

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:59.160
What are you doing sleeping here?

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:06.590
I didn't want to bother Mahiro-chan.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:10.120
If it's all right with you, 
you can come to my room.

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:18.020
Gosh, you needn't go out of your way.

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.010
Once Mahiro-san concentrates on something,

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.070
she doesn't notice a thing 
going on around her.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:25.980
It's okay. I didn't want to bother her.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.700
Once Mahiro-san decides to do something,

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.970
no matter what it is, she puts 
all her energy into doing it.

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:37.520
Of course she has failed many times.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.650
But she wouldn't be Mahiro-san otherwise.

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.990
You've been friends with her 
since you were little, right?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.390
Yes. She hasn't changed a bit.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.420
I finally made it to the end.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.700
Lion, can you read it?

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.720
Lion?

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:09.420
Huh? Where is she?

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.150
Thanks for waiting!

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:17.800
I'm finally done writing the scenario.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:18.900
Yay!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.900
Lion, thanks for looking out for me.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.660
Mahiro-san, what kind of story did you write?

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:34.240
In short, it's about about a Foreigner girl 
from Monolium who gets lost in Septpia.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.420
And she meets a girl here and they learn 
to understand each other through a song!

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.170
That sounds like a good story.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.720
And so, uh...

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.820
I'll announce the cast too.

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:48.530
There will be two staring roles.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:50.810
The girl from Septpia will be Nina.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:54.310
B-But I...

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:58.700
And the other girl from 
Monolium will be Lion.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.190
What? Me?

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.400
Please and thanks!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:04.600
Sure! Leave it to me!

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.910
Episode 8

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.910
Success Comes From Dreaming

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:45.600
So our last visit to the 
beach of the summer...

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.500
Don't talk about it.

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:50.970
Well, there wasn't a single 
soul that tried talking to us.

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:54.130
I can't hear you. I can't hear you.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:56.970
I get it, I get it. I won't 
talk about it anymore.

00:22:56.970 --> 00:22:59.870
I know! It's time for 
autumn, the season of food!

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:02.180
No way. It's still the height of late summer.

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:02.560
Autumn.

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:05.770
The season of meeting that certain someone.

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:06.480
Hi!

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:08.460
V-Vice Principal?

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:20.500
Next Episode

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:09.780
Meeting your certain someone in autumn?

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.420
Come on, autumn's when people get dumped.

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:15.280
Look at that. Seems we can't shake 
the old traditions out of you.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.390
Old?!

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.910
A quiet encounter with nature.

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:20.500
What better season than 
autumn? Don't you think?

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:23.500
As the colors of autumn deepen,

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:27.000
people seek the warmth of one another.

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.400
You too?! Wait, what does that even mean?

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.760
Autumn means Mr. Right! 
Mr. Right means autumn!

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:34.610
Let's all find our man!

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:35.560
Yeah.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:38.120
<i>Something's wrong with the 
teaching staff at this school.</i>
